    "description": "<p>For every fixed nonnegative finite integer r, we construct smooth complete metrics of strictly positive Gaussian curvature on both the plane and sphere that converge in ordinary compact-open C^r, while their unique point-normalized uniformizing diffeomorphisms fail compact-open C^(r+1) convergence. The critical r=1 case uses a small C^1 conformal correction controlling the full nonlinear inverse-coordinate curvature operator. This resolves the specified finite-integer endpoint question recorded in the 2017 Oberwolfach report, published on 3 January 2018.</p><p>The theorem concerns this specific normalized parametrization of smooth objects and makes no assertion about abstract homeomorphisms, RP^2, smooth or noninteger Holder topologies. Classical logarithmic and twisting mechanisms are credited. A bounded primary-source search through 3 October 2026 did not locate an earlier full geometric resolution, with residual risk of an earlier unindexed realization; exhaustive historical priority is not claimed. The compact support package supplies standalone manuscript source and standard-library exact finite diagnostics. Finite checks supplement the universal proof and do not certify all orders, global curvature, completeness or novelty.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in construction, derivation, drafting, adversarial review and verification. This version 1.0 preprint is unrefereed; no human peer review, journal acceptance or formal proof certification is claimed. The manuscript and new documentation are CC BY 4.0; Python code is MIT.</p>",
    "additional_descriptions": [
      {
        "description": "Preprint version 1.0. The manuscript date is 3 October 2026. Publication date is supplied by the actual upload workflow; no DOI or deposition ID is embedded. Manuscript and new documentation: CC BY 4.0. Verification code: MIT. General endpoint mechanisms are classical; historical priority qualification is explicit in the manuscript.",
        "type": {
          "id": "notes",
          "title": {
            "de": "Anmerkungen",
            "en": "Notes"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
